'''Zeekr Intelligent Technology Holding Limited''', trading as '''Zeekr Group''' ({{Lang-zh|c=|p=|l=|first=|s=极氪集团}}), is a Chinese [[Automotive industry|automobile]] company. It is wholly owned by [[Geely Automobile Holdings]].

Zeekr was founded in 2021 as a single brand specializing in [[luxury car|luxury]] [[electric car]]s. Since February 2025, the entity has become a holding company known as Zeekr Group consisting of two brands following the acquisition of [[Lynk & Co]], another brand under [[Geely Holding]].

The name of the brand is made up of "ZE" which stands for [[zero]], the starting point of infinite possibilities, "E" which stands for "evolving the electric era", and "KR" which stands for the element [[krypton]], a rare gas that emits light when electrified.<ref>{{Cite web | title=Zeekr | author = zeekregy | url=https://www.instagram.com/p/DGgUilpM0_y/ | access-date=2025-08-17 | website=Instagram}}</ref>

{{Short description|Sex characteristics between male and female}}
{{About|intersex across species from a biological perspective |humans specifically |Intersex}}
{{Distinguish|Hermaphrodite}}
{{Sex sidebar}}
'''Intersex''' is a general term for an [[organism]] that has [[Biological sex|sex]] characteristics that are between [[male]] and [[female]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=intersex {{!}} Definition & Facts|url=https://www.britannica.com/science/intersex|access-date=2021-07-10|website=Encyclopædia Britannica|language=en|quote=Intersex, in biology, an organism having physical characteristics intermediate between a true male and a true female of its species.}}</ref> It typically applies to a minority of members of [[gonochoric]] animal species such as mammals (as opposed to [[hermaphroditic]] species in which the majority of members can have both male and female sex characteristics).<ref>{{Cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=3bsgS125KH0C&q=gonochoric+intersex+encyclopedia&pg=PP3932|title=Encyclopedia of Fish Physiology: From Genome to Environment|vauthors=Farrell A|date=2011-06-01|publisher=Academic Press|isbn=978-0-08-092323-9|language=en|quote=Thus, strictly speaking, all hermaphrodites are intersex at one time point, but not all intersexes are hermaphrodites. This definition is usually applied to gonochoristic species to describe those individuals that are not normal for the species.}}</ref> Such organisms are usually [[Sterility (physiology)|sterile]].<ref name="Encyclopædia_Britannica_(2021)">{{cite web |title=Malformation – Sexual anomalies |url=https://www.britannica.com/science/malformation/Sexual-anomalies |website=Encyclopedia Britannica |publisher=Encyclopædia Britannica, Inc. |access-date=19 July 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

Intersexuality can occur due to both genetic and environmental factors<ref name="crust" /> and has been reported in [[Mammal|mammals]], [[fish]], [[Nematode|nematodes]], [[Crustacean|crustaceans]], and [[bird]]s.

{{Short description|My Little Pony pornography}} 
{{good article}}
{{Use American English|date=March 2026}}
{{Use mdy dates|date=June 2026}}
[[File:MLP clop fanart of a pony version of Wikipedia.png|thumb|A [[ponified]] version ([[ponysona]]) of [[Wikipe-tan]], the unofficial mascot of [[Wikipedia]], in a [[softcore pornography|softcore]] sexually suggestive pose]] 
{{My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic sidebar|expanded=Fandom}}
'''Clop''' (also referred to as '''''My Little Pony'' pornography''',<ref name="Dickson-2014"/><ref>{{cite book|last=Brownlee|first=Shannon|chapter=LEGO Porn: Phallic Pleasure and Knowledge |editor-last1=Hains|editor-first1=Rebecca C.|editor-last2=Mazzarella|editor-first2=Sharon R.|title=Cultural Studies of LEGO |publisher=[[Palgrave Macmillan]]|location=Cham |date=2019-11-28|pages=197–219|doi=10.1007/978-3-030-32664-7_9|isbn=978-3-030-32664-7|chapter-url=https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-32664-7_9}}</ref><ref>{{cite book |last=Fuller |first=Matthew |title=How To Be a Geek: Essays on the Culture of Software |publisher=Polity |location=Cambridge |year=2017 |page=82 |isbn=978-1-5095-1719-0 }}</ref> or '''pony porn'''<ref name="Hautakangas-2015">{{cite journal |last=Hautakangas |first=Mikko |title=It's OK to be joyful? My Little Pony and Brony masculinity |journal=Journal of Popular Television |volume=3 |issue=1 |pages=111–118 |year=2015 |doi=10.1386/jptv.3.1.111_1 |publisher=Intellect}}</ref><ref name="Burdfield-2015"/> for short) is [[erotic art|erotic]] and [[pornographic]] [[fan art]], [[fan fiction]], [[fan film]]s, [[fan game]]s, and other [[fan labor]] based on ''[[My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic]]'', ''[[My Little Pony: Equestria Girls]]'', and subsequent generations of the ''[[My Little Pony]]'' franchise. The term ''clop'' derives from the [[onomatopoeia]] for a hoofbeat and is a pun on ''[[wikt:fap|fap]]'', an Internet [[Masturbation#Terminology|slang term for masturbation]]. Related terms include ''clopfic''&mdash;a [[portmanteau]] of ''clop'' and ''fanfic'', for [[erotic fiction|erotic]] [[My Little Pony fan fiction|''My Little Pony'' fan fiction]]&mdash;and ''clopping'' for the act of masturbating to clop.

The [[brony fandom]] (the adult fandom of ''Friendship Is Magic'' that emerged on the Internet in the early 2010s) gave rise to clop alongside its other forms of [[art of the My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic fandom|fan works]]. Variously described as a subset of the brony and [[furry fandom]]s, clop has grown into one of the largest bodies of erotic fan content associated with any single media franchise. It spans visual art distributed on [[imageboard]]s, fan fiction published on [[Fimfiction]], and other fan content, including those [[generative AI|generated using artificial intelligence]] tools. [[List of My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic characters|Characters from ''Friendship Is Magic'']] are among the most frequently tagged on the furry imageboard [[e621 (website)|e621]], and the ''My Little Pony'' imageboard [[Derpibooru]] hosts hundreds of thousands of explicit images.

A source of controversy both within and outside the ''My Little Pony'' fandom, clop has been criticized by bronies and outsiders alike for sexualizing children's media; in response, bronies have taken measures to tag such works as explicit on search engines and fan sites. Fans of clop consistently distinguish it from [[zoophilia]], as their interest is directed at fictional characters perceived as sapient beings with human-like qualities, rather than at real animals. Though internal fandom surveys in 2013 suggested that only a minority of bronies have engaged in clopping, surveys in recent years have found that consumption of clop has become more widespread and accepted, with a majority of respondents in recent polls reporting that they consider explicit pony content to be a valid form of self-expression.

Clop has received substantial scholarly attention across [[sexology]], [[folklore]], [[gender studies]], [[queer studies]], and [[fan studies]]. Academics have variously interpreted clop as a form of [[queer theory|queer transgression]], an indication of the rising popularity and legitimization of [[fictosexuality]] among Western audiences, a reinforcement of traditional [[gender hierarchy|gender hierarchies]], and an eroticization of cuteness in a manner comparable to ''[[moe (slang)|moe]]'' in ''[[otaku]]'' culture.

{{Short description|Literature in the Hausa language}}
{{Use Nigerian English|date=May 2022}}
{{more citations needed|date=August 2021}}{{Islamic culture}}
'''Hausa literature''' is literature written in the [[Hausa language]].  It includes poetry, prose, songwriting, music, and drama. Hausa literature includes [[Oral literature|folk literature]], much of which has been transcribed, and provides a means of recording, preserving, and transmitting knowledge, especially in regard to social, psychological, spiritual, or political roles.

Hausa works are classified based on whether they are poetry, prose or drama. Such works are then categorized according to historical periods; otherwise, they may be classified based on their adherence to certain aesthetic features or genres.

