The '''NBA 75th Anniversary Team''', also referred to as the '''NBA 75''',<ref>{{Cite news |last=Dubose |first=Ben |date=October 19, 2021 |title=Hakeem Olajuwon, James Harden, Moses Malone, Elvin Hayes among initial NBA 75 list |work=USA Today |url=https://rocketswire.usatoday.com/2021/10/19/hakeem-olajuwon-james-harden-moses-malone-elvin-hayes-among-initial-nba-75-list/ |url-status=live |access-date=October 20, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020012722/https://rocketswire.usatoday.com/2021/10/19/hakeem-olajuwon-james-harden-moses-malone-elvin-hayes-among-initial-nba-75-list/ |archive-date=October 20, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Irving |first=Kyle |date=August 26, 2021 |title=NBA 75: Which active players could join the list of all-time greats? |work=Sporting News |url=https://www.sportingnews.com/au/nba/news/nba-75-which-active-players-could-join-the-list-of-all-time-greats/sakdvnor83l71hmwmi2s1ul1f |url-status=live |access-date=October 20, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210827000837/https://www.sportingnews.com/au/nba/news/nba-75-which-active-players-could-join-the-list-of-all-time-greats/sakdvnor83l71hmwmi2s1ul1f |archive-date=August 27, 2021}}</ref> was chosen in 2021 to honor [[2021–22 NBA season#75th anniversary promotions|the 75th anniversary]] of the founding of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). It was the fourth and most recent [[NBA anniversary teams|anniversary team]] in the league.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Jackson |first=James |date=October 22, 2021 |title=James Harden, LeBron James, Carmelo Anthony among greats celebrating place on NBA's Top 75 list |work=ESPN.com |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/32448931/james-harden-lebron-james-carmelo-anthony-greats-celebrating-place-nba-top-75-list |url-status=live |access-date=October 26, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211025200021/https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/32448931/james-harden-lebron-james-carmelo-anthony-greats-celebrating-place-nba-top-75-list |archive-date=October 25, 2021}}</ref> Similar to the [[50 Greatest Players in NBA History]] named in 1996, a panel of reporters, current and former players, coaches, general managers, and team executives selected the greatest players in league history.<ref name="nbafaq" /> Tasked with compiling a list of 75 players, the committee named an additional 76th member due to a tie in voting.<ref name="golliver_10202021">{{Cite news |last=Golliver |first=Ben |date=October 20, 2021 |title=NBA unveils 75th anniversary all-time team |newspaper=The Washington Post |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2021/10/20/nba-75th-anniversary-team/ |url-status=live |access-date=October 22, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020172059/https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2021/10/20/nba-75th-anniversary-team/ |archive-date=October 20, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Friedell |first=Nick |date=October 23, 2021 |title=Golden State Warriors rib Klay Thompson over snub from NBA's 75th anniversary team |work=ESPN.com |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/32462060/golden-state-warriors-rib-klay-thompson-snub-nba-75th-anniversary-team |url-status=live |access-date=October 24, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211024033257/https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/32462060/golden-state-warriors-rib-klay-thompson-snub-nba-75th-anniversary-team |archive-date=October 24, 2021}}</ref> It was billed as part of the league's anniversary celebration during the [[2021–22 NBA season]].<ref name="nbafaq">{{Cite web |date=October 5, 2021 |title=Everything you need to know about the NBA's 75th Anniversary Season |url=https://www.nba.com/news/nba-75-faq |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211019113624/https://www.nba.com/news/nba-75-faq |archive-date=October 19, 2021 |website=NBA.com}}</ref> Forty-five of the seventy-six players were later assembled in [[Cleveland]], during the halftime ceremony of the [[2022 NBA All-Star Game|2022 All-Star Game]].{{refn|group=note|The following players were honored posthumously: [[Paul Arizin]] (died 2006), [[Elgin Baylor]] (died 2021), [[Kobe Bryant]] ([[2020 Calabasas helicopter crash|died 2020]]), [[Wilt Chamberlain]] (died 1999), [[Dave DeBusschere]] (died 2003), [[Hal Greer]] (died 2018), [[John Havlicek]] (died 2019), [[Sam Jones (basketball, born 1933)|Sam Jones]] (died 2021), [[Moses Malone]] (died 2015), [[Pete Maravich]] (died 1988), [[George Mikan]] (died 2005), [[Dolph Schayes]] (died 2015), [[Bill Sharman]] (died 2013), [[Nate Thurmond]] (died 2016), and [[Wes Unseld]] (died 2020).<br><br>The following players were honored virtually: [[Larry Bird]], [[Bob Cousy]], [[Dave Cowens]], [[Tim Duncan]], [[Walt Frazier]], [[Karl Malone]], [[Earl Monroe]], [[Steve Nash]], [[Scottie Pippen]], [[Willis Reed]], [[Bill Russell]], [[Russell Westbrook]], and [[Lenny Wilkens]].<br><br>[[Nate Archibald]], [[Anthony Davis]] and [[Kevin Durant]] did not attend nor appear virtually in the ceremony for various reasons.}}

