'''Trump Media & Technology Group Corp.''' ('''TMTG''') is an American media and technology company headquartered in [[Sarasota, Florida]]. It runs the [[Truth Social]] social-media platform and is majority-owned by the [[Donald J. Trump Revocable Trust]].{{efn|name=trust}}

Founded by [[Andy Litinsky]] and Wes Moss in 2021,<ref name="founders1">{{Cite web |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/2024/05/31/trump-stock-price/73921010007/ |title=Trump Media stock drops in Friday trading after former president's guilty verdict |date=31 May 2024 |access-date=15 August 2025 |website=[[USA Today]] |quote=The social media company was founded by Andy Litinsky and Wes Moss in 2021}}</ref><ref name="founders2">{{Cite web |url=https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2024/sep/28/trump-media-investor-dumps-100-million-in-companys/ |title=Trump Media investor dumps $100 million in company’s shares |date=28 September 2024 |access-date=15 August 2025 |website=[[The Washington Times]] |quote=The company was founded by Andy Litinsky and Wes Moss}}</ref><ref name="founders3">{{Cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/21/business/donald-trump-wealth-trump-media.html |title=How Donald Trump’s Financial Future Became Tied to Trump Media |date=21 May 2024 |access-date=15 August 2025 |website=[[The New York Times]] |quote=Trump Media, founded by two former contestants of “The Apprentice”}}</ref> it went [[public company|public]] on March 26, 2024, after merging with [[Digital World Acquisition Corp.]] (DWAC), a [[special-purpose acquisition company]] (SPAC).<ref>{{Cite news |last1=La Monica |first1=Paul R. |last2=Clark |first2=Adam |date=March 26, 2024 |title=Truth Social Owner's Stock Soars as Trump Media Starts Trading Under DJT Ticker |url=https://www.barrons.com/articles/trump-media-truth-social-djt-stock-price-b9a7c585 |work=[[Barron's]] |url-access=subscription |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240326132104/https://www.barrons.com/amp/articles/trump-media-truth-social-djt-stock-price-b9a7c585 |archive-date=March 26, 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ft-0326">{{Cite news |last1=Gara |first1=Antoine |last2=Aliaj |first2=Ortenca |last3=Stacey |first3=Stephanie |last4=McDougall |first4=Mary |date=March 26, 2024 |title=Donald Trump has $4.6bn stake in social media group after market debut |url=https://www.ft.com/content/99f713a5-71fa-4a28-b1ee-5b6f8998887e |work=[[Financial Times]] |url-access=subscription |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240326174017/https://www.ft.com/content/99f713a5-71fa-4a28-b1ee-5b6f8998887e |archive-date=March 26, 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite news |last=Goldstein |first=Matthew |date=March 21, 2024 |title=A Little-Known Way That Trump Could Raise Money to Pay His Legal Bills |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/21/business/trump-truth-social-merger.html |work=[[The New York Times]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321190655/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/21/business/trump-truth-social-merger.html |archive-date=March 21, 2024 |url-status=live |access-date=31 December 2024 }}</ref>

In December 2025, Trump Media & Technology Group had a market cap of US$3.65 billion.<ref>{{cite news |title=Trump Media & Technology Group Corp |url=https://www.reuters.com/markets/companies/DJT.O |access-date=31 December 2025 |agency=reuters.com |publisher=reuters.com |date=31 December 2025}}</ref> By May 2026, after two quarters reporting large losses (Q4 2025, $605.5m,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.quiverquant.com/news/Trump+Media+&+Technology+Group+Corp.+(DJT)+Releases+Q4+2025+Earnings:+Large+Losses,+Flat+Revenue|title=Trump Media & Technology Group Corp. (DJT) Releases Q4 2025 Earnings: Large Losses, Flat Revenue &#124; DJT Stock News|website=www.quiverquant.com}}</ref> Q1 2026 $405.9m<ref name="Q12026">{{Cite web|url=https://www.marketwatch.com/story/trump-media-technology-group-s-1q-loss-soars-b9c7e0e1|title=Trump Media & Technology Group's 1Q Loss Soars|date=May 8, 2026|website=MarketWatch}}</ref>), the market cap was around $2.47bn.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.google.com/finance/beta/quote/DJT:NASDAQ|title=Trump Media & Technology Group Corp (DJT) Stock Price & News - Google Finance|website=www.google.com}}</ref> The company said it had ended the year with "$2.1 billion in cash, cash equivalents and short term investments."<ref name="Q12026" />

