'''Gambian literature''' consists of the oral and written literary tradition of the people of [[the Gambia]]. Oral literature, including the traditional [[griot]]s and various forms of ritual poetry, has historically been the predominant type of cultural transmission in line with the wider [[Senegambia]]. An English-language, written Gambian literature has emerged since the 1960s, spearheaded by [[Lenrie Peters]].

