[[Molybdenum]] is an essential element in most organisms.<ref name="Scottetal" /> It is most notably present in [[nitrogenase]]<ref>G.J. Leigh. Ch. 5 Structure and Spectroscopic Properties of Metallo-sulfur Clusters ''Nitrogen Fixation at the Millennium.'' Elsevier Science B. V., Amsterdam, 2002. 209-210. {{ISBN|9780444509659}}.</ref> which is an essential part of [[nitrogen fixation]].<ref>{{Cite journal |vauthors=Burris RH, Wilson PW |date=June 1945 |title=Biological Nitrogen Fixation |journal=Annual Review of Biochemistry |language=en |volume=14 |issue=1 |pages=685–708 |doi=10.1146/annurev.bi.14.070145.003345 |issn=0066-4154}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |vauthors=Streicher SL, Gurney EG, Valentine RC |date=October 1972 |title=The nitrogen fixation genes |journal=Nature |volume=239 |issue=5374 |pages=495–9 |bibcode=1972Natur.239..495S |doi=10.1038/239495a0 |pmid=4563018 |s2cid=4225250}}</ref>
